<title>USA: Century Telephone updates shareholder plan.</title>
<headline>Century Telephone updates shareholder plan.</headline>
<dateline>MONROE, La. 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Century Telephone Enterprises Inc on Tuesday updated a shareholder rights plan to replace an existing plan expiring in November.</p>
<p>The new rights will be issued as a dividend on November 1 to each common shareholder of record on September 30. The initial exercise price will be $110 per Right. The Rights expire on November 1 unless redeemed or exchanged earlier and can be exercised only if someone acquires or announces a tender offer resulting in ownership of 15 percent or more of the company's common stock.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk, 212-603-3310</p>
</text>
